---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ReceptionistWidget from '../components/ReceptionistWidget.astro';

const turnstileSiteKey = '0x4AAAAAAFpVujjoZq3bcV75';

const real = [
  'The assistant runs on a live n8n workflow with a real language model behind it.',
  'Answers are grounded in a fixed knowledge base for the fictional company, not free invention.',
  'A completed booking produces a structured lead and sends a real email notification.',
  'The page is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a rate limit, and a server-side proxy that hides the workflow endpoint.',
];

const simulated = [
  'Northgate Heating & Air does not exist. The phone number is a reserved fictional number.',
  'The three appointment windows are fixed strings, not live calendar availability.',
  'Leads are logged to a sandbox table. In a real build they go to FileMaker, a CRM, or your calendar.',
  'No payment is taken and no real appointment is created.',
];

const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Answers from a fixed knowledge base',
    body: 'Hours, services, the service area and the diagnostic fee come from one block of text. The assistant is instructed not to add facts, estimate prices, or invent availability.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Qualifies the job',
    body: 'It collects name, callback number, address, the problem in the customer\u2019s words, and a preferred window, then reads the number back for confirmation.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Hands off correctly',
    body: 'Gas smell, a carbon-monoxide alarm, no heat in freezing weather, or an active leak route straight to the emergency line, and the lead is flagged urgent.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Files the lead',
    body: 'One structured record lands in a data table and one email arrives, so nothing depends on somebody reading a chat window later.',
  },
];
---

<Layout title="AI Receptionist Demo — Jim Paul De Jose">
  <h1>AI receptionist demo</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Northgate Heating &amp; Air is a fictional HVAC company in Portland, Oregon. This is the
    receptionist it would use. Ask it for a booking and see what happens.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is the <strong>web-chat build</strong>. Phone builds run the same workflow behind a voice
    platform such as Vapi or Retell, so the part that answers, qualifies and files the lead does not
    change.
  </p>

  <ReceptionistWidget siteKey={turnstileSiteKey} />

  <p class="demo-note">
    Demo only. Do not enter real personal, medical or payment information. A message you send here is
    processed by a language model to generate a reply.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is doing</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    {
      steps.map((step) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{step.title}</h3>
          <p>{step.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <h2>What is real, and what is not</h2>
  <p>
    A demo that pretends is worth nothing, so here is the split.
  </p>

  <h3>Real</h3>
  <ul>
    {real.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h3>Simulated</h3>
  <ul>
    {simulated.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What it costs to have one</h2>
  <p>
    The package is deliberately small: one workflow, one knowledge base, one place for leads to land,
    and a handover so you can run it without me.
  </p>

  <div class="pricing">
    <div class="price-block">
      <p class="price-label">Build</p>
      <p class="price-value">$750 &ndash; $1,500</p>
      <p class="price-detail">
        Scoped by channel and integrations. Includes the knowledge base, the qualification rules, the
        lead destination, and testing against real conversations.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="price-block">
      <p class="price-label">Hosting and maintenance</p>
      <p class="price-value">$99 &ndash; $199 / month</p>
      <p class="price-detail">
        Running, monitoring, prompt and knowledge-base updates, and a monthly review of what customers
        actually asked.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Where it writes is the part that matters. A receptionist that logs a lead into a chat window is a
    chatbot. One that writes into your FileMaker system, your CRM, or your calendar is a front desk.
    That integration is the work I do.
  </p>

  <h2>How it is built</h2>
  <p>
    The conversation runs as an n8n workflow on a self-hosted instance. This page talks to it through a
    Cloudflare Pages Function that verifies a Turnstile challenge, rate-limits abuse, and keeps the
    workflow endpoint out of the page source. Leads land in a data table and arrive by email.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you want one for your business, or want to talk about wiring it into a system you already run,
    <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>

<style>
  .demo-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #6b7280;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .pricing {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .price-block {
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: #f9fafb;
  }
  .price-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6b7280;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .price-value {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111827;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .price-detail {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
